        "urlName": null
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "5b0746088fa72313783e3269",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2023-03-09T07:08:54.559Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "64043ce4fc6fa345172c4def",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 6
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This bug is the result of another bug fix. However, this is in itself an undocumented, unintended use case and only worked before due to a quirk in execution order.\n\nTo break the issue down:\n\n- Avatar author makes a single GameObject with both a Constraint and PhysBone component attached to it.\n\n- Frame begins.\n\n- The Physbones solve themselves. Gravity is enabled, so it moves downwards towards gravity.\n\n- The Constraints solve themselves. This moves the root of the chain which affects all of the bones.\n\n- Frame is rendered.\n\n*We will not be fixing this bug.* Fixing this bug would require changing the execution order of either Constraints or PhysBones, which would break a **very** large number of other avatars.\n\nAnother fix would be for us to provide a replacement Constraint system, but that is out of scope. We want to do this eventually, as native Unity Constraints have many problems, but we cannot do it now.\n\nFor now, please use this workaround:\n\nMove the Constraint component \"up\" to the parent GameObject. Leave the PhysBone component on the original GameObject. This will fix the issue.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
